/*
 * White Whale :: klone run-only config for VALDIVIESO2025_POMS_RS_EMSEQ
 *
 * Passed last, after the study config (docs/compute_profiles.md):
 *
 *   nextflow run workflows/methylation -c config/VALDIVIESO2025_POMS_RS_EMSEQ.config \
 *       -c data/studies/VALDIVIESO2025_POMS_RS_EMSEQ/klone.run.config -profile klone
 *
 * It lives under data/studies/ because a study PR may only touch that folder
 * and config/<STUDY_ID>.config (whale check-study-scope).
 *
 * Why: 40 libraries of 148-336 M pairs at 2 x 150 bp -- 2686 Gb of sequence,
 * far deeper than PESTO2022's 2 x 75 bp. At the rate ROBERTS2022 aligned on
 * klone (~6 Gb/h at 24 CPUs) every library is an estimated 7.4-16.8 h
 * (median 10.9), so NOT ONE of the 40 fits the ckpt-all window (4 h 30 m).
 * Chunked alignment is not in the workflow yet (workflows/methylation/main.nf).
 *
 * So BISMARK_ALIGN runs entirely on the lab's non-preemptible partitions,
 * spread over three lanes by a stable hash of the sample id. Unlike
 * PESTO2022's config there is no align_off_ckpt list: the condition is every
 * library. coenv cpu-g2 is used here as the third lane (docs/compute_profiles.md
 * order 3) because two lanes would run only 4 alignments at a time and this
 * study needs ~448 CPU-hours of alignment.
 *
 * KNOWN DEVIATION, accepted 2026-11-01. maxForks caps the process at 6 tasks
 * at once across all three lanes, but Nextflow has no per-queue limit, so the
 * hash can put 3 of the 6 on one lane. On coenv compute and srlab
 * cpu-g2-mem2x that cannot overrun: Slurm caps the account at 40 and 32 CPUs.
 * On coenv cpu-g2 it can -- hyakalloc reports coenv may use 928 CPUs there,
 * so the 32-CPU share in docs/compute_profiles.md is this project's
 * convention, not a Slurm limit, and it is what PESTO2022's config avoided
 * cpu-g2 for. Observed on 2026-11-01: 3 tasks, 48 CPUs and 300 GB on cpu-g2
 * against the documented 32 CPUs / 200 GB. Judged acceptable here (modest,
 * transient, and cpu-g2 had 553 of 928 CPUs free) in exchange for 6
 * concurrent alignments instead of 4, which keeps the run inside the head
 * job's 7-day wall clock. Drop the third lane to hold the convention
 * strictly, at about 5 days of alignment instead of 3.3.
 *
 * Everything else (FastQC, trimming, deduplication, extraction, summaries)
 * stays on ckpt-all as the profile has it.
 */

process {
    withName: 'BISMARK_ALIGN' {
        // Bismark's temporary FASTQ goes to the node's /scr, not the shared
        // (and often full) /gscratch.
        scratch  = '/scr'
        // 6 at once across the three lanes, not 2 per lane: see the deviation
        // note above. Slurm holds compute and cpu-g2-mem2x to 2 each; cpu-g2
        // may take more.
        maxForks = 6
        cpus     = 16
        time     = '48h'
        // Lane 0 coenv compute, 1 srlab cpu-g2-mem2x, 2 coenv cpu-g2.
        memory         = { [ '90 GB', '251 GB', '100 GB' ][ Math.floorMod(sample_id.hashCode(), 3) ] }
        queue          = { [ 'compute', 'cpu-g2-mem2x', 'cpu-g2' ][ Math.floorMod(sample_id.hashCode(), 3) ] }
        clusterOptions = { [ '--account=coenv', '--account=srlab', '--account=coenv' ][ Math.floorMod(sample_id.hashCode(), 3) ] }
    }
}
